---
const steps = [
  "Scan files",
  "Analyze files",
  "Build the dependency graph",
  "Detect the framework",
  "Detect routes",
  "Detect the database",
  "Extract entities",
  "Detect capabilities",
  "Detect features",
  "Infer the domain",
  "Rank critical files",
  "Generate flows"
];
const optionalAi = "Infer the domain";

const frameworks = [
  "Next.js", "Astro", "Nuxt", "SvelteKit", "Remix", "React Router", "TanStack",
  "Expo Router", "SolidStart", "Qwik City", "Angular", "Express", "Fastify", "Hono",
  "Elysia", "Koa", "AdonisJS", "NestJS"
];
---

<section class="method page" aria-labelledby="method-title">
  <div class="method__intro">
    <h2 class="method__title" id="method-title">
      The same code gives the same map.
    </h2>
    <p class="method__copy">
      Files, imports, routes, features and flows come from static analysis, so
      the result doesn't change between runs. AI is optional and is used in
      three places: inferring what the project is for, describing files, and
      answering questions. If the provider fails, <code>devmap analyze</code>{" "}
      still finishes.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="method__steps" aria-label="What devmap analyze does, in order">
    {steps.map((step) => (
      <li>
        {step}
        {step === optionalAi && <span class="method__ai"> (optional AI)</span>}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <div class="method__support">
    <section>
      <h3>Routes mapped for</h3>
      <p>{frameworks.join(", ")}.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Read with full syntax trees</h3>
      <p>TypeScript, JavaScript, Vue, Svelte and Astro.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h3>Read with pattern matching</h3>
      <p>Python, PHP, Go, Ruby, C# and Java: imports, exports and declarations.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .method {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem);
    padding-block: var(--section-space);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .method__intro {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .method__intro {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
      align-items: start;
    }
  }

  .method__title {
    max-width: 11em;
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    line-height: 1.02;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
  }

  .method__copy {
    max-width: 38rem;
    padding-top: 0.6rem;
  }

  .method__copy code {
    font-size: 0.875em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .method__steps {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    counter-reset: step;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  @media (min-width: 40rem) {
    .method__steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      column-gap: 2rem;
    }
  }

  @media (min-width: 62rem) {
    .method__steps {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .method__steps li {
    padding-block: 0.85rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink);
    counter-increment: step;
  }

  .method__steps li::before {
    content: counter(step, decimal-leading-zero);
    display: inline-block;
    width: 3ch;
    margin-right: 1ch;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .method__ai {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .method__support {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem 3rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .method__support {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
  }

  .method__support h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .method__support p {
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
    color: var(--text);
  }
</style>
